% ============================================================================
% abo-genotype-antigen.query.adj — worked recall over the biology
% ABO-genotype/antigen causal-composition library.
% ============================================================================
% The shape a learner (or an LLM) produces to ANSWER "which antigen(s) does
% an ia_ib genotype's blood carry?" — it states no biology fact of its own —
% it only `import`s the grounded rule and asks binding queries. The answer is
% DERIVED, composing abo-genotype-phenotype's specific genotype->phenotype
% assignment with blood-groups' general phenotype->antigen mapping, so every
% answer carries BOTH citations in its `steps` trail. The last query
% demonstrates honest abstention: `ia_i` (a heterozygote with the null
% allele) is a real ABO genotype, but `abo-genotype-phenotype.adj` itself
% never states its phenotype in continuous prose, so this derived rule
% inherits that same abstention rather than guessing.
%
% Run (from this directory so the relative import resolves):
%     ../../../../packages/rust/target/debug/adj-lang-cli abo-genotype-antigen.query.adj
% ============================================================================

import "abo-genotype-antigen.adj"

? abo_genotype_antigen(ia_ia, $Antigen)          % expect a_antigen (direct)
? abo_genotype_antigen(ib_ib, $Antigen)          % expect b_antigen (direct)
? abo_genotype_antigen(ia_ib, $Antigen)          % expect a_and_b_antigens (direct)
? abo_genotype_antigen($G, a_and_b_antigens)     % expect ia_ib (reverse)
? abo_genotype_antigen(ia_i, $Antigen)           % expect abstain -- abo_genotype_phenotype itself abstains on ia_i
